How can you programmatically determine which profiles are currently active in a Spring Boot application?
-->
1.In Spring Boot, you can determine the active profiles programmatically using the Environment
@Component
public class ProfileChecker {

    @Autowired
    private Environment environment;

    @PostConstruct
    public void checkActiveProfiles() {
        String[] activeProfiles = environment.getActiveProfiles();
        System.out.println("Active profiles: " + Arrays.toString(activeProfiles));
    }
}

environment.getActiveProfiles() returns an array of currently active profiles.
If no profile is explicitly set, Spring uses the default profile, accessible via environment.getDefaultProfiles().


2.Using @Value annotation:

@Value("${spring.profiles.active:default}")
private String activeProfiles;

3.
Using ApplicationContext:

@Autowired
private ApplicationContext context;

public void checkProfiles() {
    String[] profiles = context.getEnvironment().getActiveProfiles();
}


