How to enable actuator in spring boot 

Add spring-boot-starter-actuator dependency.
Configure which endpoints to expose in application.properties or application.yml.
Access endpoints via /actuator/*.

Step 1: Add the dependency
If you’re using Maven, add:

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
</dependency>


For Gradle:
implementation 'org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-actuator'


Step 2: Enable endpoints in application.properties or application.yml
By default, only a few endpoints like /health and /info are exposed. You can enable others:

# Enable all actuator endpoints
management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=*

# Optional: set actuator port different from app
# management.server.port=8081


Or using YAML:
management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: "*"  # expose all endpoints


Step 3: Access Actuator endpoints
After starting the app, you can access endpoints like:
http://localhost:8080/actuator/health → checks app health
http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics → metrics data
http://localhost:8080/actuator/info → app info


